Wait — a detail: pushing the same mail twice back-to-back. First pushMail starts a turn (`_runTurn`). Second pushMail is deduped (same from+text) — dropped. So exactly one turn. 

But there's a race subtlety: two identical pushes; deduper keyed on from+text, not message id. AC18 invariant = "dedup-by-message-id" (conceptually; implementation keys from+text). Fine.

Another subtlety: does the user message_done arrive on the ui-v2 wire before or... The host emits user message_done at turn start (message_done role user), then assistant streams + message_done assistant. Poll handles ordering.

Also the wire envelope: `{kind:'message_done', message:{role, text, ...}}` — `_translate` removes 'type' from the event and spreads the rest, so message has role/text.

One more consideration: boot — in app mode, does booting need a reload for the app to attach? Irrelevant for our probe: we connect after boot.

Also: does `fa.panel.evaluate` chrome.runtime.connect work in the app iframe page? The app page is at chrome-extension://id/panel/app/index.html — extension origin, chrome.runtime available. Yes.

